#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:0
msgid ""
"View, set, retrieve, and unset configuration options for installed snaps, "
"including nested values, JSON output, and validated updates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:8
msgid "Configure snaps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:10
msgid ""
"Certain snaps, such as those providing a background service, have "
"configuration options that can be viewed and changed. The commands for "
"viewing and changing these configuration options are `snap get`, `snap set` "
"and `snap unset`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:12
msgid ""
"To see the configuration options of an installed snap, enter `snap get <snap "
"name>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:14
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap get nextcloud\n"
"Key        Value\n"
"mode       production\n"
"nextcloud  {...}\n"
"php        {...}\n"
"ports      {...}\n"
"private    {...}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:24
msgid ""
"The `{...}` in the output indicates that there are further options beneath "
"the current key name level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:27
msgid ""
"If there are no configuration options, you will see `error: snap <snap name> "
"has no configuration`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:30
msgid ""
"To explore configuration options, append the key name to the *get* command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:32
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap get nextcloud ports\n"
"Key          Value\n"
"ports.http   80\n"
"ports.https  443\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:39
msgid ""
"Alternatively, the entire set of configuration options can be dumped as JSON "
"by adding the `-d` option:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:41
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap get -d nextcloud\n"
"{\n"
"        \"http\": {\n"
"                \"compression\": false\n"
"        },\n"
"        \"mode\": \"production\",\n"
"        \"nextcloud\": {\n"
"                \"cron-interval\": \"5m\"\n"
"        },\n"
"        \"php\": {\n"
"                \"memory-limit\": \"512M\"\n"
"        },\n"
"        \"ports\": {\n"
"                \"http\": 80,\n"
"                \"https\": 443\n"
"        },\n"
"        \"private\": {\n"
"                \"http\": {\n"
"                        \"compression\": false\n"
"                },\n"
"                \"mode\": \"production\",\n"
"                \"nextcloud\": {\n"
"                        \"cron-interval\": \"5m\"\n"
"                },\n"
"                \"php\": {\n"
"                        \"memory-limit\": \"512M\"\n"
"                },\n"
"                \"ports\": {\n"
"                        \"http\": 80,\n"
"                        \"https\": 443\n"
"                }\n"
"        }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:77
msgid "Use the *set* command to change a configuration option:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:79
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap set nextcloud ports.http=81\n"
"$ sudo snap get nextcloud ports\n"
"Key          Value\n"
"ports.http   81\n"
"ports.https  443\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:87
msgid ""
"To clear and return a value to its default state, use the *unset* command  "
"(from _snapd 2.41+_):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:88
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap unset nextcloud ports.http\n"
"# sudo snap get nextcloud ports\n"
"Key          Value\n"
"ports.http   80\n"
"ports.https  443\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:96
msgid ""
"Adding an exclamation mark (`!`) to the end of an option name  also clears "
"its value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:98
msgid "$ sudo snap set nextcloud ports.http!\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:102
msgid ""
"Un-setting with an exclamation mark can be mixed with setting other options "
"at the same time:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:104
msgid "$ sudo snap set nextcloud ports.https! ports.http=81\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:108
msgid ""
"The update process will test the validity of the configuration options. If "
"any errors are detected, the overall change is cancelled and the previous "
"configuration reinstated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/configure-snaps.md:110
msgid ""
"Similarly, if the configuration update process takes longer than a "
"reasonable amount of time, currently 5 minutes, the update is forcefully "
"aborted and the once again the configuration is rolled back."
msgstr ""
